# Compoise Android release signing template

Copy this file to `android/key.properties` (or
`android/app/key.properties`), replace the placeholder values
with the real release credentials, and keep it out of Git: `.gitignore` already
ignores `key.properties`, `keystore.properties`, `*.jks`, `*.keystore`, `*.pfx`
and `*.p12`.

`storeFile` is resolved the way `android/app/build.gradle.kts` resolves it: an
absolute path is used as declared, otherwise it is looked up under
`android/app/` first and then in the directory holding this file. So
`release.jks` means `android/app/release.jks`, which is also the layout the CI
workflow writes together with `android/key.properties`.

```properties
keyAlias=matrixflow-release
keyPassword=REPLACE_WITH_KEY_PASSWORD
storePassword=REPLACE_WITH_STORE_PASSWORD
storeFile=release.jks
```

Notes:

- Create the keystore yourself with `keytool` and keep the file plus its
  passwords outside the repository. Do not commit the filled file and do not
  paste its values into issues, CI logs or documentation.
- In CI the workflow builds the same files from repository secrets
  (`ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64`, `ANDROID_STORE_PASSWORD`, `ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD`,
  `ANDROID_KEY_ALIAS`) and deletes them again after the build.
- Without these credentials `scripts/build_release.ps1 -Platform Android`
  refuses to build, because a debug-signed APK must never be published as a
  formal release.
